{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b9e7635a-a3b2-468a-b190-0aee33005e30","step":{"id":"s1","script":"In y equals m x plus b, b is the y-intercept. Here the line crosses the y-axis at one.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Slope-intercept form"},{"op":"equation","id":"general","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"y=mx+b"},{"op":"figure","id":"graph","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-1,3],"y":[-2,7],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"intercept","at":[0,1],"label":"b = 1"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b9e7635a-a3b2-468a-b190-0aee33005e30","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The slope m is rise divided by run. From the intercept, move right one and up two: the slope is two.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"slope_marks","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"corner","at":[1,1]},{"kind":"point","id":"next","at":[1,3],"label":"(1, 3)"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"intercept"},"to":{"at":"corner"},"arrow":true,"stroke":"dashed","label":"run 1"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"corner"},"to":{"at":"next"},"arrow":true,"stroke":"dashed","label":"rise 2"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"slope","anchor":{"el":"general","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"m=\\frac{\\text{rise}}{\\text{run}}=\\frac{2}{1}=2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b9e7635a-a3b2-468a-b190-0aee33005e30","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Draw the straight line through these points. With slope two and intercept one, its equation is y equals two x plus one.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"draw_line","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"line","y":"2*x+1","domain":[-1,2.8]}]},{"op":"equation","id":"specific","anchor":{"el":"slope","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"y=2x+1"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"For x = 2, what is y on this line?","expected_gist":"y = 5"}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b9e7635a-a3b2-468a-b190-0aee33005e30","step":{"id":"s4","script":"At x equals two, multiply by the slope and add the intercept. The result is five, matching the point on our line.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"check_point","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"result","at":{"on":"line","x":2},"label":"(2, 5)"},{"kind":"segment","from":[2,0],"to":{"at":"result"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[0,5],"to":{"at":"result"},"stroke":"dashed"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"substitute","anchor":{"el":"specific","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"x=2\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad y=2(2)+1=5"}],"checkpoint":null}}
